From: Yaron Shahrabani <yarons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: Cancel the buffers of a request whose capture was cancelled

When the capture buffer of a frame fails or is cancelled (every time the
camera stops) and a converter or the software ISP is in use, the request
at the head of the conversion queue is completed with its user-facing
buffers untouched. Their metadata still says FrameSuccess, so the request
completes as RequestComplete, with stale pictures and without
SensorTimestamp.

The Android HAL forwards that as a shutter notification with timestamp 0.
The camera service never retires such a frame ("flushInflightRequests:
Frame 191 | Timestamp: 0, metadata arrived: true, buffers left: 0"), and
closing the camera waits for its 5 s drain timeout: switching between the
cameras took 6 to 15 s. Mark the buffers as cancelled.

Also return the buffers of the HAL when a request is aborted.
---
--- a/src/android/camera_device.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_device.cpp
@@ -952,9 +952,16 @@
 {
 	notifyError(descriptor->frameNumber_, nullptr, CAMERA3_MSG_ERROR_REQUEST);
 
-	for (auto &buffer : descriptor->buffers_)
+	for (auto &buffer : descriptor->buffers_) {
 		buffer.status = Camera3RequestDescriptor::Status::Error;
 
+		/* No post-processing will return the buffer of the HAL. */
+		if (buffer.internalBuffer) {
+			buffer.stream->putBuffer(buffer.internalBuffer);
+			buffer.internalBuffer = nullptr;
+		}
+	}
+
 	descriptor->status_ = Camera3RequestDescriptor::Status::Error;
 }
 
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #include "libcamera/internal/delayed_controls.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/device_enumerator.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/formats.h"
+#include "libcamera/internal/framebuffer.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/global_configuration.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/media_device.h"
 #include "libcamera/internal/pipeline_handler.h"
@@ -910,9 +911,16 @@
 		if (conversionQueue_.empty())
 			return;
 
+		/*
+		 * Nothing is written to the user-facing buffers: mark them as
+		 * cancelled, or the request completes as a successful one, with
+		 * stale pictures and without sensor timestamp.
+		 */
 		const RequestOutputs &outputs = conversionQueue_.front();
-		for (auto &[stream, buf] : outputs.outputs)
+		for (auto &[stream, buf] : outputs.outputs) {
+			buf->_d()->cancel();
 			pipe->completeBuffer(outputs.request, buf);
+		}
 		SimpleFrameInfo *info = frameInfo_.find(outputs.request->sequence());
 		if (info)
 			info->metadataRequired = false;
